    Fence KVM child wait publication
    
    [hermit2, degraded-unresolved, gpt-5.6-sol, devbig014, role=impl]
    
    Fence concurrent parent waits across the Tool callback prefix and logical
    waitability commit. Plain running children keep WNOHANG behavior, while an
    announced terminal transition cannot leak a host-preemption-dependent zero.
    
    Classify descendant teardown from the exact direct parent's logical terminal
    state. A terminal transitive root no longer auto-reaps a grandchild away from
    its still-live parent, and direct-parent teardown retires its exact family
    edges.
    
    Add forced wait4/waitid fence coverage, failed-publication wake coverage, and
    real-KVM root-terminal matrices for waitable, SIG_IGN, and SA_NOCLDWAIT paths.

